global._fc=global._J6;_n5._gc=(-1);_n5._hc=(-1);global._ic=false;_n5._jc=false;_n5._kc="HOW TO PLAY\n\nTHE BOARD is the decks of two ships side by side as the two crews battle at sea: your crew starts at the bottom, the enemy crew at the top. Each column is a lane.\n\nGOAL: get one of your figures to the far end of a lane to turn that lane's light (at the top) green. Turn 3 of the 4 green to win. The enemy has to turn all 4 of yours (at the bottom) green.\n\nYOUR TURN\n- UNITS (shown under your deck) are what you spend to place cards. Each card costs units. They refill every turn, and you get more as the fight goes on and for each lane where you have more figures.\n- DRAWING is free and optional: click your deck once per turn to draw.\n- To place a figure, click a card, then a glowing tile on your front row.\n- END YOUR TURN with the token (left of the ship) or Space. You can end it without drawing or playing anything.\n- Cards only stay in your hand for 3 turns (orange = last turn).\n\nTHE BATTLE: after the enemy places its figures, every figure moves forward by itself and attacks the enemy in front of it. Your 2 home rows give +1 HP; the enemy's 2 rows give +1 attack.\n\nTHE DAGGER (next to your deck): click it, then one of your own figures on your first two rows, to remove that figure and free up its spot.\n\nCOINS AND SHOPS: winning a fight earns coins (more for each light you turned green). Between fights you stop at port shops to spend coins on items. Items sit beside the ship; click one on your turn to use it. Coins are only for shops; units are only for placing cards in a fight.\n\nTIPS: hover cards, figures and items to see what they do. \"DEATH\" means a figure won't survive the next battle. Right-click cancels. Escape pauses.";
